h(2, id: "cli") { 2. Command line }

p { The binary is named code{docup}. Commands: }

codeblock(lang: "text", file: "usage", line_numbers: true) {!
docup build <input.du> [flags]
docup watch <input.du> [flags]
docup fmt [path] [--check] [--stdout]
docup new <directory> [flags]
docup init [flags]
docup version
docup help
!}

p { With no command, the compiler prints help and exits 1. code{docup -v}, code{docup --version}, and code{docup version} print the version string. code{docup -h}, code{docup --help}, and code{docup help} print usage. }

p { Color in the terminal is on when stdout is a terminal and code{NO_COLOR} is unset. Otherwise ANSI codes are omitted. }

h(3, id: "flags") { 2.1 Shared flags }

p { Used by code{build} and code{watch}: }

table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Flag }
    cell { Meaning }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-o}, code{--output} }
    cell { Output HTML path. Default is the input path with the extension changed to .html. If the input has no extension, code{.html} is appended. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-s}, code{--style} }
    cell { Path to a CSS file. Contents are copied into code{<style id="docup-custom-css">}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-p}, code{--port} }
    cell { Watch-mode port only. Default 8080. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-v}, code{--verbose} }
    cell { Print elapsed time for each build stage. On build and watch, code{-V} is accepted as an alias for code{-v}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{-q}, code{--quiet} }
    cell { Hide stage progress and the success summary. }
  }
}

p { code{--verbose} and code{--quiet} cannot be used together. }

h(3, id: "build") { 2.2 build }

p { Compiles once and writes the HTML file. A missing or unreadable input file is a fatal error. An empty file (only ASCII whitespace) is a fatal error. If the input does not use a .du extension, the compiler prints a warning and continues. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup build report.du
docup build report.du -o dist/index.html -s style.css
docup build report.du --verbose
!}

h(3, id: "watch") { 2.3 watch }

p { Compiles once, writes the output file, then binds code{127.0.0.1:<port>}. It polls watched files every 250 ms. On change it rebuilds. A failed rebuild leaves the last page in place and keeps watching. }

p { If the first compile fails, the server still starts. The page body is a short HTML error placeholder until a later compile succeeds. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup watch report.du
docup watch report.du --port 3000
!}

p { Watched paths are the root source file, every successfully resolved include, and the code{--style} file if one was given. }

h(3, id: "dev-server") { 2.4 Dev server }

p { The watch server accepts GET only. Other methods return 405. }

table {
  row(header: true) {
    cell { Path }
    cell { Response }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{/}, code{/index.html} }
    cell { Current compiled HTML, with a live-reload EventSource script inserted before code{</body>}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { code{/docup-events} }
    cell { Server-sent events. A rebuild writes code{data: reload}. }
  }
  row {
    cell { any other path }
    cell { File under the input file's directory, if it exists. Otherwise 404. }
  }
}

p { Asset Content-Type is chosen from the file extension: html, css, js, json, png, jpg, jpeg, gif, svg, webp, ico, woff, woff2, ttf. Anything else is code{application/octet-stream}. }

h(3, id: "fmt") { 2.5 fmt }

p { Parses a .du file and writes it back in canonical form. Default path is the current directory. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup fmt
docup fmt docs
docup fmt index.du
docup fmt --check
docup fmt index.du --stdout
!}

list {
  item { With no flags, files that differ are rewritten. }
  item { code{--check} prints paths that need formatting and exits 1 if any do. Nothing is written. }
  item { code{--stdout} prints one formatted file to stdout. It cannot be used on a directory. }
  item { code{--check} and code{--stdout} cannot be used together. }
}

p { Directory walks skip hidden names and the folders code{target}, code{node_modules}, and code{dist}. Only files with a .du extension are formatted. }

p { Canonical form: four-space indent, meta keys in a fixed order then alphabetical leftovers, blank line between top-level blocks, prose wrapped near 80 columns. code{fmt} parses first; a parse error is reported and that file is skipped. }

h(3, id: "new-cmd") { 2.6 new }

p { Creates a directory and writes a starter project. The directory must not exist, or must be empty. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup new my-doc
docup new my-doc --title "Report" --author "Name" --theme textbook --desc "Notes" -y
!}

p { Flags: code{--title}, code{--author}, code{--theme}, code{--desc}, and code{-y} / code{--yes} to skip prompts. Without code{--yes}, and when stdin and stdout are terminals, the command asks for title, author, theme, description, and whether to include sample sections. }

h(3, id: "init-cmd") { 2.7 init }

p { Same files as code{new}, written into the current directory. Aborts if code{index.du} already exists. }

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
docup init
docup init --theme nord -y
!}

p { Files written when missing: code{index.du}, code{style.css}, code{.gitignore}, code{README.md}. Theme names accepted by these commands: code{textbook}, code{default}, code{sepia}, code{nord}, code{solarized}. An unknown theme falls back to textbook. }
